---
description: Canonical model design constraints for Stage 03
alwaysApply: true
---

Stage 03 is **design only** unless explicitly moved to an implementation gate.

Forbidden in design phase:

- creating a canonical database;
- writing SQL DDL;
- running ETL or migrating rows;
- merging patients across Source A and Source B;
- creating global_patient_id or global_subject_id;
- modifying artifacts under artifacts/stage-01/ or artifacts/stage-02/;
- promoting CANDIDATE or HYPOTHESIS mappings to CONFIRMED clinical semantics;
- treating POTENTIAL_OVERLAP as proof of subject equality;
- promoting stage-03-design-report.md to FINAL;
- cross-source consolidation of birthdate, sex, or gender;
- automatic normalization of source sex/gender to biological_sex.

Required design invariants:

- three separated layers: evidence (OBSERVED…IMPUTED), simulation (SYNTHETIC), prediction (PREDICTED);
- every canonical entity carries provenance metadata;
- raw values are preserved after normalization;
- Subject identity is source-local: source_system + source_subject_key;
- stable demographics use SubjectCharacteristic with raw characteristic codes;
- REFERENCE_CATALOG facts are not patient clinical events;
- IdentityLinkEvidence is future-only and must not activate merge;
- ScenarioIntervention holds identity and defaults; ScenarioEvent applies timeline overrides per scenario_event_precedence_contract;
- state snapshot construction follows state-snapshot-contract.yaml (design contract only);
- canonical record construction follows record-construction-contract.yaml (design contract only);

Mapping status semantics:

- CONFIRMED_SCHEMA confirms structure only, not clinical equivalence;
- UNRESOLVED and HYPOTHESIS from Stage 02 must be preserved, not silently resolved.

When editing Stage 03 artifacts, update design-content-manifest.sha256 via stage-03-check.
Content artifact list is STAGE03_CONTENT_ARTIFACTS in the verifier (do not hardcode file counts separately).
